{
  "index": 19,
  "response": "**Step 1: Divide the balls into 3 groups of 4.**\n\n- Place 4 balls on one side of the balance scale and 4 balls on the other side.\n- The side with the heavier ball identifies the group with the odd ball.\n\n\n**Step 2: Identify the odd ball within the heavier or lighter group from Step 1.**\n\n- Take the 4 balls from the side that contained the heavier group in Step 1 and pair them with the remaining 4 balls from that group.\n- The side with the heavier ball identifies the odd ball within that group.\n\n\n**Step 3: Determine if the odd ball is heavier or lighter.**\n\n- Weigh the odd ball against one of the remaining 8 balls.\n- If the odd ball is heavier, it is the heavier ball. If the odd ball is lighter, it is the lighter ball.",
